Phase 0 — Decisions (1–2 hours)
- Confirm Supabase project + connection details.
- Decide: single-user placeholder vs real auth now.
- Confirm transport: Server Actions first, with service layer to enable future Route Handlers.
- Outcome: agreed stack + ownership strategy.

Phase 1 — Infrastructure (half day)
- Add Prisma + DATABASE_URL.
- Init Prisma schema + migrations.
- Create base users/workspaces tables (even if single-user).
- Outcome: DB connected, migrations working.

Phase 2 — Core Schema (half day)
- Align schema with existing types:
  - projects with name, status, statusText, papers, progress, created, modified.
  - protocols JSONB (full protocol object).
  - drafts JSONB (full draft state).
  - studies (ledger) relational.
- Add ownerId/workspaceId to all rows.
- Outcome: schema matches UI and is multi-user ready.

Phase 3 — Service Layer (1 day)
- Create server-only modules: lib/server/projects.ts, protocols.ts, ledger.ts, drafts.ts.
- Add validation + ownership checks.
- Outcome: reusable logic for Server Actions or APIs.

Phase 4 — Projects + Protocol (1–2 days)
- Implement save/load for projects & protocol via Server Actions (or Route Handlers).
- Update contexts to call backend instead of localStorage.
- Outcome: core persistence works end-to-end.

Phase 5 — LocalStorage Migration (half day)
- On first load, detect localStorage data and upload to DB.
- Clear/mark migrated state.
- Outcome: no data loss for current users.

Phase 6 — Ledger (1–2 days)
- Implement study CRUD + syncing.
- Connect ledger UI to DB.
- Outcome: relational queries working; filters and counts stable.

Phase 7 — Draft (1–2 days)
- Store full DraftState JSONB (not just content).
- Hook draft UI to DB with debounced saves.
- Outcome: full draft persistence.

Phase 8 — Copilot State (optional)
- Decide canonical copilot source (project vs per-section).
- Store messages with context fields.
- Outcome: copilot state persists across sessions.

Phase 9 — Files + Exports (optional)
- Add blob storage for PDFs/exports.
- Store file metadata in DB.
- Outcome: ready for reference detail pages + exports.
- Import Study decisions:
  - Storage: Supabase Storage bucket for PDFs.
  - Flow: attach PDF to an existing Study (no create-on-import).
  - Access: public for now.
  - Duplicates: allow (no warning yet).
  - Metadata: manual only for now (no auto-extract).

Phase 10 — Multi-user enablement (when ready)
- Add auth provider.
- Replace placeholder ID with real userId/workspaceId.
- Enforce ownership in all queries.
- Outcome: multi-user without schema rewrite.
- Report: Codex quality/architecture report written to codex-quality-report.md (2026-02-02).
